{"ts":"2026-07-19T07:51:50.116Z","type":"finding","frontier":"spread-cure-at-target-minting-gap-main","claim":"Live run 2026-07-19T07-22-01: after the surplus drain COMPLETED (REMOVE c98831ba done 07:18:57, over-target window only 36s), the partition sat at target 3 replicas on 2 distinct nodes with authoritative inventory UNAVAILABLE — the sealed spread-cure scenario — for 3 minutes to timeout. The planner minted spread ADDs typed plain spread_replicas because classifyPriorityExpandForSpreadCureCondition requires naturalReplaceCount>=1 (no natural REPLACE candidate exists post-drain at exact target) plus five exact count equalities (occupied/deficit/voter/active === target; lagging accounting rows can break these), so the cure declined SILENTLY in its own target state; the topology guard denied every untyped ADD replica_inventory_unusable and the conservative-union escape ignores non-cure moves. Same failure shape as TiKV PD issue 6559 (exact-state escape rule missing a neighboring composite state; see solve/artifacts/priority-spread-peer-research/).","kind":"root-cause","evidence":"test-output/reports/movielens-lagrange-service-affinity-live-2026-07-19T07-22-01-510Z.report.json","rulesOut":null,"verification":null,"regressionClassification":null,"scopePressureClassification":null}
